# Wiki sync on commit

The ops dashboard **Wiki** tab (`dashboard/src/wiki/content.ts`, rendered by `dashboard/src/pages/Wiki.tsx`) is the operator-facing mirror of how the bot works. Treat it like setup docs: do not leave it stale when behavior changes.

## Before finishing a commit

1. Diff the change set. Ask: does this alter scanning, sleeves, entry/exit priorities, follow mode, sizing/risk brakes, HALT, dashboard tab meaning, update/approve flow, or accounting?
2. If **yes**, update the matching Wiki section(s) in **`dashboard/src/wiki/content.ts`** in the same commit (surgical edits — do not rewrite untouched sections).
3. If the change is also a public/setup fact, still apply `docs-sync-on-commit.mdc` (site / setup / llms).
4. If STRATEGY.md is the source of truth for a strategy change, update STRATEGY.md **and** the Wiki section that mirrors it.

## When Wiki almost always needs a pass

- New/changed P0–P5 rules, follow gates, sleeves, Kelly/circuit/cluster/regime knobs
- New dashboard tabs or Halt / Errors / Changes / Settings behavior operators must understand
- New blacklist / skip classes or accounting definitions shown in Activity
- Kill-switch / HALT semantics

## Do not

- Duplicate full SETUP/Railway install into the Wiki (link Docs instead)
- Paste secrets, keys, or live `DASH_TOKEN` values
- Skip Wiki because “STRATEGY.md is enough” — operators use the dashboard Wiki

## Done means

Strategy/ops commits include Wiki updates when operator-visible behavior drifted (or an explicit “no wiki impact” judgment).
